  "query_preview": "..\n(Friday Night through Thursday)\nIssued at 1127 PM CDT Thu Oct 8 2026\n\nDry and unseasonably warm weather will continue through early next\nweek as an upper ridge remains over the area. The remnants of\nHurricane Isaias will remain well to our east, with little impact\nto the weather in our area, although afternoon highs may be\nslightly cooler Saturday.\n\nSouth winds will increase later this weekend into next week,\nleading to an increase in fire weather concerns. The upper ridge\nwill move east of the area next week, with the upper flow becoming\nsouthwest. This will result in increasing shower and thunderstorm\nchances during the middle to latter part of next week, with an\napproaching cold front helping to focus the higher rain chances.\nTemperatures will remain warm through the middle of the week, and\nincreasing humidity levels will make it feel quite humid as well.\nCooler weather looks to finally arrive by the end of next week\nonce the cold front passes.",
